--  Configuration pragmas for every Landin unit, in both build modes.
--
--  Each is a restriction: it forbids a construct the compiler does not
--  use, so the binder refuses a unit that starts using it, and GNAT may
--  then leave out the support the construct would need.  None suppresses
--  a check.  compiler/ada/TOOLCHAIN.md says why each is here.

--  No task is ever aborted, so finalizing a controlled object, which every
--  container reference and tampering lock is, need not defer abort.
pragma Restrictions (No_Abort_Statements);
pragma Restrictions (Max_Asynchronous_Select_Nesting => 0);

--  Nothing maps an external tag back to a type, so a tagged type need not
--  enter the runtime's tag table when its unit is elaborated.
pragma Restrictions (No_Tagged_Type_Registration);
